--- Windows backend (added 2026-09-26) ---

Same commit, e72da2b53805894878023d01949a25a082e0a5cb. License re-verified at
the source on 2026-09-26: the repository LICENSE (Apache-2.0) and NOTICE are
byte-identical to the copies here, and codex-rs/Cargo.toml declares
license = "Apache-2.0" for the workspace, which windows-sandbox-rs inherits.

Ported (subset, rewritten against windows-sys 0.61 with errors propagated)
into crates/kgraf-sandbox/src/sandbox/windows.rs:
  codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/src/token.rs
      restricted token for the unelevated backend: flags DISABLE_MAX_PRIVILEGE
      | LUA_TOKEN | WRITE_RESTRICTED; restricting SIDs in the order
      capabilities, logon SID, Everyone; default DACL of logon SID GENERIC_ALL
      plus OWNER RIGHTS READ_CONTROL; SeChangeNotifyPrivilege enabled.
  codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/src/acl.rs
      WRITE_ALLOW_MASK (read, write, execute, DELETE, no FILE_DELETE_CHILD)
      inherited by descendants; the deny-write ACE on a protected child.
  codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/src/cap.rs
      capability SID shape S-1-5-21-a-b-c-d, one SID per writable root.
  codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/src/desktop.rs
      private desktop whose DACL admits the logon SID.
  codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/src/process.rs, proc_thread_attr.rs
      CreateProcessAsUserW with lpDesktop set, STARTF_USESTDHANDLES and an
      explicit PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_HANDLE_LIST.

Deliberately different from upstream:
  - ACL, desktop and token failures are errors. Upstream ignores several
    (`let _ = ...`), which would run a command with less confinement (SR-008).
  - Capability SIDs are derived from the root path (FNV-1a) instead of drawn
    at random and persisted in a state file.
  - The root itself gets no DELETE (an explicit non-inherited ACE plus an
    inherit-only ACE), so it cannot be moved or removed.
  - The deny-write mask omits the SYNCHRONIZE and READ_CONTROL bits of
    FILE_GENERIC_WRITE.
  - The job is joined through CREATE_SUSPENDED plus AssignProcessToJobObject
    instead of PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_JOB_LIST; every UI limit is set.
  - No global NUL-device DACL change and no offline-network environment
    rewrite (proxy variables are not isolation).
  - A private desktop reused per workspace (not per spawn and not a global
    cache), on the process's own window station (queried, not a hard-coded
    WinSta0), so scheduled and service runs work.
  - The default DACL grants the user SID and a fresh per-spawn SID (also a
    restricting SID), never the logon SID, so one spawn's process tree cannot
    be opened for write by another same-session sandbox.
  - The token integrity level is dropped to Low and each writable root and the
    private desktop are labeled Low, so mandatory integrity control blocks
    writes up to Medium objects and UIPI blocks SendInput to the user's
    desktop. Upstream's unelevated backend does not use integrity levels.
  - Reparse points on a root or its `.git` are refused, a root on a
    non-ACL volume is refused, and effective write is verified with
    AccessCheck under the restricted token (upstream does none of these).

Not taken:
  - codex-rs/windows-sandbox-service/ (whole crate) and the elevated backend
    in windows-sandbox-rs (setup*.rs, identity.rs, wfp*.rs, elevated*,
    provisioning*, hide_users.rs): they create a dedicated local user,
    firewall (WFP) filters and a Windows service, all of which need
    administrator rights. kGraf's constraint is no admin and no installer
    (sandboxing evidence 2026-09-24). That path is also the only upstream one
    that denies reads and network; its absence is why the kGraf Windows
    backend reports partial isolation.
  - deny_read_*.rs: upstream itself refuses deny-read under a
    WRITE_RESTRICTED token ("this backend cannot make capability-SID
    deny-read ACLs authoritative").
  - conpty/, unified_exec/, stdio_bridge.rs: interactive sessions, out of
    scope for the runner.

